{
    "background_story": "Alejandra crossed the border with her family when she was just a teenager, seeking a better life and fleeing the violence that ravaged her hometown. Despite her resilience and determination, she grew up in the shadows, always looking over her shoulder, fearful of being discovered. As an undocumented immigrant, Alejandra's future seemed uncertain, and she struggled to find her place in a society that often seemed hostile. Yet, she persevered, working multiple jobs to support her family and pursuing her passion for art in secret. Alejandra's talent eventually caught the attention of a local gallery owner, who offered her a chance to showcase her work. Though she risked exposure, Alejandra's art became a powerful voice for the undocumented community, shedding light on the struggles and triumphs of those living in the margins.",
